0556+  247E             ;******************************************************************
0557+  247E                 .sbttl "Position All Maze Objects"
0558+  247E             ;******************************************************************
0559+  247E             ;* Moves and controls all objects in
0560+  247E             ;* the maze.
0561+  247E             ;*                                     
0562+  247E             ;* Inputs: Object X,Y, Status, VelX & Y 
0563+  247E             ;*                                      
0564+  247E             ;* Output: Update position and status.  
0565+  247E             ;*                                      
0566+  247E             ;* Uses:   (see movthg)                 
0567+  247E             ;*         +2 additional bytes stack    
0568+  247E             ;*******************************************************************
0569+  247E             ;* objst notes:
0570+  247E             ;* 
0571+  247E             ;* objst is the main object status byte. There are some general
0572+  247E             ;* rules about this and then each object may use the status byte
0573+  247E             ;* in specific ways for that object. Each object objst is described
0574+  247E             ;* below with the code to move that object.
0575+  247E             ;*******************************************************************
0576+  247E             ;* General objst usage:
0577+  247E             ;*
0578+  247E             ;*  00 = Object is dead/not-active or otherwise ignored
0579+  247E             ;*  80 = Object is in the process of dying, it does not affect Rex
0580+  247E             ;*  40 = Object should be drawn if this is set, this I believe
0581+  247E             ;*       is a flag to save cpu time on drawing an object each time.
0582+  247E             ;*       It is called the 'Screen Flag' in other areas
0583+  247E             ;*  10 = Means that this is a 'temp object' which when checked against
0584+  247E             ;*       wall collisions, it will be set to destroyed objst = $80
0585+  247E             ;*
0586+  247E             ;*  01 or Greater = Active for drawing and collision detection
0587+  247E             ;*******************************************************************
0588+  247E             ;* Fireball/Spark objst Notes:
0589+  247E             ;*
0590+  247E             ;* Bit $10 
0591+  247E             ;*     Set: Fireball was launched from a Trip Pad (red dude) or IonCannon shot
0592+  247E             ;*     Clr: Just a normal old spark (white)
0593+  247E             ;*******************************************************************
0594+  247E AD 3F 07    posmo   lda tspark              ;Beaming, move nothing... woo hoo!
0595+  2481                     \ .push  *, 0 \ BEQ  * 
0595+  2481             
0595+  2481 F0 FE       
0596+  2483 4C F9 2C                jmp ?drtran         	;Skip all drawing routines transporter
