2930+  33E6             ;***********************************************************
2931+  33E6             ;* Ths routine decides if it's time to draw 
2932+  33E6             ;* a 'thing' on the screen or not. This is  
2933+  33E6             ;* done by checking the 'things' position   
2934+  33E6             ;* with the current screen location. If     
2935+  33E6             ;* within certain limits, the object is     
2936+  33E6             ;* placed on the screen at its location -   
2937+  33E6             ;* the screen location.                     
2938+  33E6             ;* Note: The upper left corner is 0,0 and   
2939+  33E6             ;* the maze is built in the fourth quadrant 
2940+  33E6             ;* so all objects should have X positive    
2941+  33E6             ;* and Y negative.                          
2942+  33E6             ;*                                          
2943+  33E6             ;* Inputs: (x) = object number              
2944+  33E6             ;*         objxl,objxh,objyl,objyh=location 
2945+  33E6             ;*  If X > ztop then xlsb from table lsb    
2946+  33E6             ;*  in maze.                                
2947+  33E6             ;*                                          
2948+  33E6             ;* Output: (y)= 80 if object placed, else 0 
2949+  33E6             ;*                                          
2950+  33E6             ;* Uses:   temp1, xmot                      
2951+  33E6             ;***********************************************************
2952+  33E6 A0 00       locate  ldy #00                 ;Will set it to 80 if placed
